---
import HarmonicExplorer from './HarmonicExplorer.svelte'
import MandelbrotExplorer from './MandelbrotExplorer.svelte'
import StaticPlot from './StaticPlot.astro'
---

<section class='visualization-examples' aria-labelledby='visualization-examples-title'>
  <h2 id='visualization-examples-title'>Visualization foundation</h2>
  <p>
    These examples keep the first render useful: exact geometry and the data plot are static
    HTML/SVG, while the harmonic model adds behavior only after it becomes visible.
  </p>
  <StaticPlot />
  <HarmonicExplorer client:visible={{ rootMargin: '200px' }} />
  <MandelbrotExplorer client:visible={{ rootMargin: '200px' }} />
  <figure class='geometry-sample'>
    <svg viewBox='0 0 320 170' role='img' aria-labelledby='geometry-title geometry-description'>
      <title id='geometry-title'>Exact decision geometry</title><desc id='geometry-description'
        >A triangle with vertices A, B, and C and a blue median from A to the midpoint of BC.</desc
      >
      <path d='M35 140 L160 25 L285 140 Z' class='shape'></path><path
        d='M160 25 L160 140'
        class='median'></path>
      <circle cx='35' cy='140' r='3.5'></circle><circle cx='160' cy='25' r='3.5'></circle><circle
        cx='285'
        cy='140'
        r='3.5'></circle><circle cx='160' cy='140' r='3.5'></circle>
      <text x='20' y='159'>B</text><text x='155' y='17'>A</text><text x='291' y='159'>C</text><text
        x='165'
        y='159'>M</text
      >
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <strong>Post-local pattern.</strong> An article with exact geometry can keep its SVG and typed calculation
      beside the post, as Pikurn does, without introducing a shared runtime.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<style>
  .visualization-examples {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    font-family: var(--wow-font-text, monospace);
  }
  .visualization-examples > p {
    max-width: 70ch;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .geometry-sample {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--wow-border);
    background: var(--wow-back-alt);
  }
  .geometry-sample svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 36rem;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--wow-text);
  }
  .shape {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .median {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--wow-link);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }
  circle {
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  text {
    fill: currentColor;
    font-family: var(--wow-font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
